# Virtual comparison: the numerical endpoint is not a whole burette step.
# Both vessels contain 0.0023 mol HCl. At 0.1 mol/L, equivalence requires
# approximately 23 mL. The 7 mL trial increment deliberately misses it.
# The automatic solver refines its last increment; a physical burette and
# indicator have their own uncertainty, which this calculation does not model.
register lv3
add v1 water 200mL
add v1 HCl 0.0023mol
titrate v1 NaOH 0.1M 7mL until ph 7
measure v1 ph
new
add v2 water 200mL
add v2 HCl 0.0023mol
titrate v2 NaOH 0.1M 1mL until ph 7
measure v2 ph
inspect
